[h2]Polaris interface update[/h2]
Optional shared Polaris controls reuse native button artwork, provide secondary-click actions and wrap navigation at narrow widths. Existing interfaces remain compatible.
Browser checks do not establish Unity interaction approval. The recent refresh pacing remains in place; further performance recordings are deferred.

[h2]Polaris readability correction[/h2]
Dark button faces now keep labels readable in every interaction state. This fixes the white-button regression reported in game. The corrected native appearance still awaits owner playtesting.

[b]Item handling correction[/b]
Add opt-in native transport-action normalization shared by content mods: retain useful actions, add missing pickup/drop, match stack actions to stack limits and keep installed machinery out of carry slots. Restore declared cumbersome flags in detached load data for explicitly registered bulky cargo. Preserve saved hand placement until successful native release, then retire the legacy hand attachment. No save files, contents, mass, wear or progress are rewritten. Live menu and inventory handling remain owner-tested.

[b]Merchant and salvage update[/b]
Add a shared stock-coverage helper that fills omitted item offers without duplicating an already prepared lot or replacing its condition. Existing merchant inventories, native pricing and other providers remain untouched. Normal restocking and new loot generation are required; existing inventories stay as they are. Offline checks are not gameplay validation.

[b]Item-action audit[/b]
The complete item-action audit now checks generated native maintenance actions and saved cargo relationships as well as declared actions. Shared safety checks can withhold dismantling for cargo, work lots or stack members. This documentation update does not change runtime behaviour.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/development/item-handling-audit.md]Complete findings and item ledger[/url]

[h2]Assembly and maintenance update[/h2]
Shared construction-site support and read-only item/maintenance information preserve native work and save handling.
Offline checks are not Unity gameplay approval. See [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/section-assembly-and-maintenance.md]assembly and maintenance instructions[/url].

[h2]Finding current instructions[/h2]
Use the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/README.md]operating-guide index[/url] for current controls and requirements. Dated research and design records retain their original scope; they are not installation instructions.

[b]Construction appearance[/b]
Optional section-construction stages follow delivered parts and saved work without changing construction requirements. Private marker materials preserve native geometry and selection effects; unchanged stages do not rewrite materials. Offline checks pass; Unity visuals remain unverified.
